<title>DENMARK: Danish April North Sea gas production falls 29 pct.</title>
<headline>Danish April North Sea gas production falls 29 pct.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Danish Underground Consortium (DUC) production of gas from its North Sea fields fell 29.0 percent in April 1997 to 491 million cubic metres from 695 million cubic metres in March, a spokesman for operator A.P. Moeller Group told Reuters on Tuesday.</p>
<p>    (Million cubic metres)   April 97    March 97   April 96</p>
<p>    Total production	     491	  695	  474</p>
<p>DUC is responsible for virtually the entire output from Denmark's North Sea oil and gas fields which make the country the fourth-biggest offshore gas producer in western Europe after Norway, Britain and the Netherlands.</p>
<p>A.P. Moeller Group owns 39 percent of DUC. Its two partners, Royal Dutch/Shell group and Texaco Inc own 46 percent and 15 percent respectively.</p>
<p>--Chris Follett, Copenhagen Newsroom 45-33-969652</p>
</text>
